# 14. XR technology strategy

For the web experience, use WebXR where supported. WebXR provides the AR/VR session layer, while the actual rendering and 3D asset management comes from your graphics stack. ([MDN Web Docs][4])

Your implementation should detect:

```text
Does browser support WebXR?
        │
   ┌────┴────┐
   YES       NO
    │         │
    ▼         ▼
WebXR       3D viewer
AR/VR       2D site
```

The XR API itself supports modes such as `immersive-ar`, `immersive-vr`, and `inline`; immersive sessions also require appropriate permissions and user initiation. ([MDN Web Docs][5])

So don't build the platform around the assumption that every visitor has a headset.

