# 15. The secret sauce: shared state

This is where the whole thing gets interesting.

The same object should exist across:

**Web → AR → VR → AI → Cart → Order**

For example:

```text
PRODUCT #9281
      │
      ├── Website representation
      ├── 3D model
      ├── AR representation
      ├── VR representation
      ├── AI knowledge
      ├── product page
      ├── cart item
      └── order item
```

So when a user places a virtual grow light in their AR room:

```text
AR OBJECT
    ↓
PRODUCT ID 9281
    ↓
GROW PLAN
    ↓
CART
    ↓
ORDER
```

There should never be separate "AR products" and "commerce products."

There should be **one canonical product identity with multiple representations**.

